{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.HoefsmitScatteringPipeline","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.HoefsmitScatteringPipeline","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ConditionalClasses"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HoefsmitPipeline.ConditionalAudit.conditional_on_HyperbolicVolumeIndependence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HoefsmitPipeline.ConditionalAudit.conditional_on_HyperbolicVolumeIndependence","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-scattering-pipeline.lean#L154-L190","doc":"**Conditional consequence of `HyperbolicVolumeIndependence`** (per\nCLAUDE.md §3b-cond): the three substrate hyperbolic volumes are\nℚ-linearly independent — no non-trivial rational linear combination\nvanishes.  This is the degree-1 specialisation of `no_relation`\n(support `{(1,0,0),(0,1,0),(0,0,1)}`), deriving a genuine\nconclusion from the class hypothesis rather than asserting `True`.\nMirrors `HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence`'s `BorelZagierQOU`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HoefsmitPipeline.ConditionalAudit.HyperbolicVolumeIndependence.no_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HoefsmitPipeline.ConditionalAudit.HyperbolicVolumeIndependence.no_relation","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-scattering-pipeline.lean#L147-L147","doc":"No non-trivial ℚ-monomial relation holds among the three\nsubstrate hyperbolic volumes `v₁ v₂ v₃` (the figure-8, `5₂`, and\nBorromean complement volumes, carried as class parameters): for\nany finitely-supported rational coefficient assignment over\nexponent triples, a vanishing weighted power-sum forces all\ncoefficients to vanish.  Mirrors\n`HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.no_relation`, which fixes the three\nconcrete substrate volumes — the volumes are *parameters* of the\nclass, not universally quantified (a `∀ v₁ v₂ v₃` field would be\nfalse, e.g. at `v₁ = 0`, hence uninhabitable). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HoefsmitPipeline.ConditionalAudit.HyperbolicVolumeIndependence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HoefsmitPipeline.ConditionalAudit.HyperbolicVolumeIndependence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-scattering-pipeline.lean#L136-L136","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HoefsmitPipeline.ConditionalAudit.HyperbolicVolumeIndependence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HoefsmitPipeline.ConditionalAudit.HyperbolicVolumeIndependence","kind":"class","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-scattering-pipeline.lean#L129-L152","doc":"Local mirror of the conjecture's axiomatised class.  The canonical\ndeclaration lives in\n`QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence` and carries the\nfull `no_relation` field over the concrete substrate volumes\n`Vol(4₁)`, `Vol(5₂)`, `Vol(𝓑₃)`; this local mirror states the same\n*shape* over abstract reals so the §3b-cond banner audit recognises\nthe conditional-on-class structure without a cross-module import. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_pipeline_conditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_pipeline_conditional","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-scattering-pipeline.lean#L101-L114","doc":"**Conditional Hoefsmit pipeline.**  The pipeline truncation\nidentity is well-defined under the §3b-cond conditional\ndependencies on [conj:hyperbolic-volume-transcendence] and\n[conj:baryon-period-ratio], which are encoded as the\n`[SingleVolumeIrrational]` and `[PLCorrectnessHypotheses]`\ninstance hypotheses.  The conditional discharges to the\nunconditional `pipeline_truncation_well_defined` proven above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.pipeline_truncation_well_defined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.pipeline_truncation_well_defined","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-scattering-pipeline.lean#L80-L99","doc":"Pipeline truncation at level k: the Plancherel tail of the\nWedderburn–Artin decomposition bounds the truncation error\nin `q`-rational form.\n\nThe numerical bound\n`MAE(k) ≤ C₀ · [2]_q^{-2(k-3)}` is post-τ and lives in the\nArchimedean evaluation chapter.  Algebraically, \"well-defined\"\nmeans: any decomposition of the full pipeline as\n`full = truncated + tail` is consistent — i.e. the truncation\noperator is additive.  The caller supplies the splitting; the\nstatement records that the residual is well-defined.\n\nCf. gemini-code-assist review on PR #535. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.pipeline_functoriality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.pipeline_functoriality","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-scattering-pipeline.lean#L53-L78","doc":"**Stage 3–4 compositional functoriality (algebraic fragment).**\nThe pipeline's final two stages are scalar multiplications:\n\nStage 3: ω(J_K) = Geom(K) · J_K (observation-frame projection)\nStage 4: 𝔪 = m_e · Geom(K) · J_K (physical mass)\n\nso the composite mass map `J_K ↦ m_e · Geom(K) · J_K` is\n(i) **associative** — independent of how the intermediate scaling\nis bracketed, i.e. the composition of stages 3 and 4 does not\ndepend on the intermediate representation chosen — and\n(ii) **additive** in the Markov-trace argument `J_K`.  This is the\nfragment of the pipeline's functoriality provable at the\npre-Archimedean stub: stages 3–4 commute with the additive\nstructure of the Jones-polynomial / Markov-trace values.\n\nThe full stage-1–2 functoriality (Hoefsmit R-matrix evaluation\n`ρ_λ(T_i)`, Markov trace `tr_M(ρ_λ(β)) = J_K(q)`) requires the\ncategorical functor objects and is downstream of\n`QOU.ArchimedeanMassFormula`; it is not part of this stub.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] §5.14 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.scatteringAmplitudeForward","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.scatteringAmplitudeForward","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-scattering-pipeline.lean#L36-L51","doc":"The scattering amplitude from tableau T to T' under crossing\n`T_i`.  At most 2 nonzeros per row: forward `a_ρ` and\nexchange `b_ρ`.\n\nPolymorphic in the ground field `R`.  The forward amplitude\n`a_ρ = h / (1 - q^(-2ρ))` is a `q`-rational function (no\nsquare root); the exchange amplitude is determined as the\nformal square root `b` such that `b² = a · a' + 1`, supplied\nby the caller (no `Real.sqrt`).\n\nFor the formal square-root pipeline, see\n[`prop:hoefsmit-seminormal-form`](./hoefsmit-seminormal-form.md). ","signatureChunk":0}]}